      {
        "id": "p93-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the largest domain of $f$ that contains $5$, so that $f^{-1}$ exists.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$[3,\\infty)$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=x^2-6x\\\\f(x)&=(x-3)^2-9\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe vertex is $(3,-9)$. The right branch contains $5$ and passes the horizontal line test, so the largest interval is $[3,\\infty)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the equation of $f^{-1}(x)$ in this domain.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f^{-1}(x)=3+\\sqrt{x+9}$, where $x\\ge-9$.",
          "worked": "Interchange $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=(y-3)^2-9\\\\x+9&=(y-3)^2\\\\\\sqrt{x+9}&=y-3\\\\y&=3+\\sqrt{x+9}\\end{align*}$$\n\nChoose the positive root because $y\\ge3$. Hence $f^{-1}(x)=3+\\sqrt{x+9}$, with domain $[-9,\\infty)$, the range of the restricted $f$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p93-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the coordinates of the point where the graph of $y=f(x)$ intersects $y=f^{-1}(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p93-q5-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
